## Instructions
- You are read-only: do not change any file. Your deliverable is the structured report.
- Report what the evidence above shows, not what the plan hoped for. A worker whose run is `dead` or `closed` delivered nothing, however good its subtask sounded.
- Put every subtask that failed, was closed, or delivered less than it claimed in `gaps`. A report that hides a missing branch is worse than no report: someone will merge the rest and believe the change is complete.
- You may read the repository to check what the branches claim to do, but you cannot see the workers' branches themselves — say so in `unknowns` rather than guessing at their contents.
- Set `merge_order` only when one branch must land before another; leave it empty when they are independent.
